Thank you. I must admit I...

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:31.260
I do touch it up a bit.

00:58:31.540 --> 00:58:39.540
Would you go in now, please?

00:58:39.740 --> 00:58:39.920
Sure.

00:58:43.800 --> 00:58:44.620
Oh, no, sweetheart.

00:58:44.820 --> 00:58:45.180
Not now.

00:58:45.420 --> 00:58:45.960
Why not?

00:58:46.440 --> 00:58:47.460
My name is Rattigan.

00:58:47.970 --> 00:58:48.510
Your name, please?

00:58:48.850 --> 00:58:49.590
Elaine Froman.

00:58:49.950 --> 00:58:51.390
Could you show me some sort of identification?

00:58:52.010 --> 00:58:53.880
I could, but why should I?

00:58:55.060 --> 00:58:56.300
Would you look at this card again, please?

00:58:57.540 --> 00:58:59.060
Office of Internal Security.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:01.840
This involves the security of our country.

00:59:02.000 --> 00:59:03.120
Now, I'd like to see some identification.

00:59:03.720 --> 00:59:04.040
Of course.

00:59:09.590 --> 00:59:15.200
Driver's license, credit cards, and credentials from my company.

00:59:15.770 --> 00:59:17.590
I'm a buyer for Langvance in New York.

00:59:18.730 --> 00:59:19.330
Where's your coat?

00:59:19.940 --> 00:59:20.840
The stewardess has it.

00:59:21.520 --> 00:59:22.340
I'd like to see it.

00:59:28.680 --> 00:59:29.500
My coat, please.

00:59:34.440 --> 00:59:35.840
How much longer is the point of no return?

00:59:37.140 --> 00:59:37.820
Less than an hour.

00:59:38.420 --> 00:59:38.920
Give him a call.

00:59:41.690 --> 00:59:44.020
Transorient 12, Los Angeles Center.

00:59:52.010 --> 00:59:53.770
Bought this coat in New York, Miss Roman?

00:59:54.100 --> 00:59:55.500
I got it in New York.

00:59:55.800 --> 00:59:57.240
I'm a buyer, Mr. Rattigan.

00:59:57.720 --> 00:59:59.540
A buyer never buys anything for a coat.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:01.620
Mr. Rattigan to the flight deck.

01:00:03.620 --> 01:00:04.200
Excuse me.

01:00:15.260 --> 01:00:15.860
This is Rattigan.

01:00:16.310 --> 01:00:19.070
Rattigan, they tell me you're less than 40 minutes from the point of no return.

01:00:19.210 --> 01:00:19.870
What have you found out?

01:00:20.410 --> 01:00:21.450
Two of the women check out.

01:00:22.060 --> 01:00:23.540
The third one calls us up, Jean Myers.

01:00:23.640 --> 01:00:24.400
I'll go to work on her.

01:00:24.680 --> 01:00:25.360
Get busy, will ya?

01:00:25.580 --> 01:00:26.400
You don't have much time.

01:00:26.730 --> 01:00:27.090
Yes, sir.

01:00:30.410 --> 01:00:37.070
Would you mind?

01:00:52.110 --> 01:00:57.840
You say your name is Gene Myers.

01:00:58.490 --> 01:00:59.030
Can you prove it?

01:00:59.190 --> 01:00:59.650
Of course.

01:01:00.760 --> 01:01:03.380
I have a driver's license and some traveler's checks.

01:01:05.710 --> 01:01:09.130
Well, I must have left them in my other purse.

01:01:10.020 --> 01:01:11.740
And where is your other purse?

01:01:12.370 --> 01:01:14.010
I packed it in my suitcase.

01:01:15.660 --> 01:01:18.680
I can certainly identify myself as soon as we get to Honolulu.

01:01:19.120 --> 01:01:20.580
I won't do. I have to find out now.

01:01:20.900 --> 01:01:21.500
Find out what?

01:01:23.840 --> 01:01:28.040
Miss Myers, there is a species of fungus that threatens the Earth today.

01:01:28.910 --> 01:01:29.970
Discover Dr. Palmer.

01:01:30.160 --> 01:01:36.840
called it blood rust. I've seen the blood rust. It killed the man who discovered it.

01:01:37.750 --> 01:01:43.050
Saw what was left of him. The woman I'm looking for may be a carrier of this stuff. She was the

01:01:43.050 --> 01:01:48.080
woman who was with Palmer the day before he was killed. Now, are you that woman? No, I swear I'm

01:01:48.080 --> 01:01:53.830
not. Give me your baggage check. I'll have to get your suitcase. If your story about the other

01:01:53.830 --> 01:01:56.940
purse isn't true, you might as well tell me now. It is true.

01:02:05.630 --> 01:02:17.720
Gotta get into the baggage compartment. You have to go through the emergency hatch. Jim take them back

01:02:31.020 --> 01:02:34.940
gentlemen i'm sorry to disturb you will you please move forward i need this area clear

01:02:34.940 --> 01:02:57.800
find any empty seat man want why does he keep bothering us he says there's some horrible stuff

01:02:57.800 --> 01:02:59.900
called blood rust that it could destroy the earth

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:00.960
if it ever got started.

01:03:01.420 --> 01:03:03.260
He thinks one of us might be a carrier.

01:03:04.620 --> 01:03:06.620
Blood rust killed a man who discovered it.

01:03:14.040 --> 01:03:15.100
I'm the woman you're looking for.

01:03:16.140 --> 01:03:17.060
I was with Dr. Palmer.

01:03:18.070 --> 01:03:19.130
Tell the captain to turn back.

01:03:19.270 --> 01:03:20.370
Get whatever orders you need,

01:03:20.450 --> 01:03:21.490
but get this ship turned around.

01:03:57.830 --> 01:03:58.930
It's just a precaution.

01:04:01.470 --> 01:04:01.990
Black tank.

01:04:03.160 --> 01:04:03.780
Button it up.

01:04:04.060 --> 01:04:15.830
This is Radegan speaking.

01:04:16.440 --> 01:04:16.900
Found it.

01:04:17.400 --> 01:04:18.260
Yeah, I found her, right?

01:04:18.320 --> 01:04:19.240
I found blood rust, too.

01:04:19.320 --> 01:04:20.680
The baggage compartment's crawling with it.

01:04:21.160 --> 01:04:23.340
Try to keep the stuff confined to the baggage compartment.

01:04:23.950 --> 01:04:24.890
Is the captain listening in?

01:04:25.430 --> 01:04:25.750
Affirmative.

01:04:26.070 --> 01:04:26.590
Captain here.

01:04:26.910 --> 01:04:29.110
Captain, I'm going to have to get you down as quickly as possible.

01:04:29.470 --> 01:04:29.970
Well, Santa Barbara...

01:04:30.060 --> 01:04:34.620
our first landfall. How about Santa Barbara Airport? No, they don't have the facilities I need.

01:04:34.900 --> 01:04:53.760
Make it the Oxnard Air Force Base. Oxnard Air Force Base. Afraid to come near me? No. I've been in

01:04:53.760 --> 01:04:58.130
contact with the blood rest too, Mrs. Greenland. Why did you run?

01:05:00.540 --> 01:05:05.070
When I saw the story about Dr. Palmer dying in a fire, I thought that's why they wanted me.

01:05:05.270 --> 01:05:07.740
I couldn't get involved in a scandal.

01:05:09.070 --> 01:05:11.700
You see, I've got a husband I love very much.

01:05:11.860 --> 01:05:15.630
This isn't a police matter, Mrs. Greeley.

01:05:16.860 --> 01:05:19.400
All Mr. Hand wants to do is destroy the blood rest.

01:05:20.600 --> 01:05:23.720
He's not interested in exposing your past. He'll probably never even use your name.

01:05:25.840 --> 01:05:26.640
I hope you're right.

01:05:28.220 --> 01:05:28.380
Sure.

01:05:42.820 --> 01:05:44.070
12, go ahead.

01:05:44.520 --> 01:05:46.040
When will you make Oxnard Air Force Base?

01:05:46.510 --> 01:05:55.740
Stand by, please. Orient 12, estimating Oxnard Air Force Base, 0540.

01:05:56.320 --> 01:05:59.970
5.40 a.m. There'll be just enough daylight for us to see what we're doing.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:00.140
one.

01:07:26.970 --> 01:07:27.190
please.

01:07:31.190 --> 01:07:33.520
All this stuff is getting into the ship!

01:07:46.460 --> 01:07:47.260
Cabin pressure is dropping.

01:07:48.230 --> 01:07:49.470
Disengage the superchargers.

01:07:50.220 --> 01:07:51.920
Notify ATC this is an emergency.

01:07:54.880 --> 01:07:57.420
Cabin pressure is down fast.

01:07:57.700 --> 01:07:59.840
This stuff must have forced to open the outside baggage door.

01:08:30.700 --> 01:08:32.300
Estimate ten minutes, Oxnard.

01:08:32.640 --> 01:08:35.420
Bring her in as close to the emergency unit as you can.

01:08:35.780 --> 01:08:36.200
Will do.

01:08:39.372 --> 01:08:40.552
Can't get our landing gear down.

01:08:41.292 --> 01:08:43.152
Rudrust must have damaged the hydraulic system.

01:08:43.820 --> 01:08:44.760
That's for making a belly landing.

01:08:45.260 --> 01:08:46.220
North-South runway.

01:08:46.956 --> 01:08:48.376
We'll lay a fomite path for you.

01:08:49.036 --> 01:08:51.036
Power! Acknowledge formite! Pass!

01:08:51.308 --> 01:08:51.668
All right.

01:10:35.980 --> 01:10:36.980
End of the movie
